11.11 Sale Analytics — Sprint Plan

Project Goal

Build a big data analytics application for a Manila-based online seller to analyze one million simulated 11.11 sale orders. The application will identify top-selling product categories, regional sales patterns, peak order hours, and cancellation rates, then present the findings in a Streamlit dashboard with an AI-generated sales briefing.

User Stories and Acceptance Criteria

1. Store Owner

User story:As a store owner, I want to see total revenue, total orders, average order value, and cancellation rate so that I can evaluate the performance of the 11.11 sale.

Acceptance criteria:

1. The dashboard displays total revenue from delivered orders, total orders, average order value, and cancellation rate using the cleaned dataset.
2. The dashboard displays revenue by product category and allows the user to filter the regional sales view by region.

2. Marketing Team

User story:As a marketing team member, I want to identify peak ordering hours and top-performing product categories so that I can improve the timing and targeting of future promotions.

Acceptance criteria:

1. The dashboard displays an hourly order chart that includes the November 11 midnight and evening sale spikes.
2. The category summary ranks product categories by delivered-order revenue and can be exported as a CSV file.

3. Delivery Partner

User story:As a delivery partner, I want to understand order volumes by region and COD cancellation patterns so that I can plan delivery capacity and reduce avoidable failed deliveries.

Acceptance criteria:

1. The analysis reports order counts by region and cancellation rates by payment method, including COD.
2. The report identifies regions with high order volumes and presents cancellation findings without automatically excluding COD customers.

